{
  "schema": 1,
  "description": "The versioned export both apps write and read (docs/backup.md, spec story 91). 'current': the format name and version this build writes. 'order': the tables an export carries, in the order a restore applies them, which is the synced-tables order, so a row is written after whatever it points at. 'checks': what a reader makes of a file's header and rows before it changes anything; null means the file is fine, and any other value is the one reason it is refused, nothing being written either way. 'takesFile': whether a restore takes the file's row over the local one, by the server updated_at both carry, which is the rule sync already uses; a row that is not there locally is always taken. 'golden': one small export as the document and as the exact text both apps write, so a file from the phone reads on the PC and the other way around. Tombstones are left out of an export, so a row may point at something the file does not carry; that is not an error.",
